        "Do not spend money you cannot afford to lose. Start with a budget that fits a predefined test limit. Ad platforms change campaign structures and optimisation behaviour, so check current Meta guidance and account settings before implementation.\nWhat to define before a test\n- Hypothesis: which desire might resonate and why?\n- Audience: who is the message for?\n- Creative: what image and copy will communicate it?\n- Offer: what exactly is being sold?\n- Landing page: does it match the ad?\n- Budget: what is the maximum test spend?\n- Duration: what observation window is reasonable?\n- Decision rule: what evidence will make you stop, revise, or continue?\nDo not judge a test by one metric\nReview:\n- Impressions and reach.\n- CPM.\n- Link click-through rate.\n- Cost per landing-page view.\n- Add-to-cart rate.\n- Initiate-checkout rate.\n- Purchase conversion rate.\n- Cost per purchase.\n- Average order value.\n- ROAS.\n- Contribution after advertising.\n- Refunds and cancellations.\nA high click-through rate with no purchases may mean the ad is attracting curiosity rather than qualified buyers. A weak conversion rate may indicate a mismatch between the ad and the landing page, a poor offer, trust concerns, or a checkout problem."
