        "The transcript does not provide a time-tracking breakdown showing exactly how those four hours were allocated. It also does not establish that four hours is sufficient for every store or at every stage. A new store may require more time for research, supplier communication, creative production, customer support, and troubleshooting.",
        "The useful operating principle is to keep the workflow focused and use tools to reduce repetitive setup work—without outsourcing judgment or responsibility.\nExample four-hour operating block\nThis is a suggested schedule, not the speaker's documented schedule.\nTime\tWork block\tMain output\n30 min\tP&L and campaign review\tDaily financial picture and issues\n45 min\tCustomer support and fulfilment\tOrders checked; customer issues resolved\n60 min\tCreative and offer iteration\tNew or improved test assets\n45 min\tProduct and competitor research\tResearch notes and next hypotheses\n30 min\tStore quality and analytics\tFixes and conversion observations\n30 min\tSupplier and operations\tStock, delivery, and quality follow-up",
